y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20631, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016pXsmjx9ivtLPZgNrn82dS", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20631, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01LidufgnHHNQVcXwYXrL92S", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20931, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01LidufgnHHNQVcXwYXrL92S", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20931, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LidufgnHHNQVcXwYXrL92S", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 26095, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01VxjTyqefm9GTNwQ3qJCkkz", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after it was deployed to production in all regions (error rate 18%). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. The agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on mixed versions for a short time. A retry finished the rollback. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and review why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56695, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01VxjTyqefm9GTNwQ3qJCkkz", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56695, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01VxjTyqefm9GTNwQ3qJCkkz", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58395, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RWdnGGVWFuoVwmjaE9RpQv", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58695, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RWdnGGVWFuoVwmjaE9RpQv", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58695, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RWdnGGVWFuoVwmjaE9RpQv", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63939, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n1. **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing version is v2.3.1, which had an 18% error rate. Its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. INC-0001 is a SEV2 for checkout-api and is open. It explains what happened and the rollback, and lists follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and review why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HzJttpoQUGA5JwSmkHaqEW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CRe3EBXwp74CwELGmBqp8B", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KHcE2ixVUtN6qRHXhHAYWH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01E3JeMDMLRncFPDCX83NMBR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll retry the rollback once. It's idempotent for us-east.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01E9qL5mD2Tw263zX45hH6GC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016pXsmjx9ivtLPZgNrn82dS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LidufgnHHNQVcXwYXrL92S", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VxjTyqefm9GTNwQ3qJCkkz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 began failing health checks after it was deployed to production in all regions (error rate 18%). v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. The agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left regions on mixed versions for a short time. A retry finished the rollback. All regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error during the rollback, and review why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RWdnGGVWFuoVwmjaE9RpQv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n1. **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing version is v2.3.1, which had an 18% error rate. Its release candidate was also unhealthy in staging.\n2. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1. I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are now all on v2.3.0, health checks pass and the error rate is about 0.2%. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 has been healthy in production before.\n3. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one incident and the on-call engineer was paged once. INC-0001 is a SEV2 for checkout-api and is open. It explains what happened and the rollback, and lists follow-ups: find why v2.3.1 failed, look into the orchestrator error, and review why a release that failed in staging was promoted to production.", "type": "text"}]}]}